  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two spheres <math><mi>P</mi></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> of equal radii have densities <math><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , respectively. The spheres are connected by a massless string and placed in liquids <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> of densities <math><msub><mrow><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and viscosities <math><msub><mrow><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> , respectively. They float in equilibrium with the sphere <math><mi>P</mi></math> in <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and sphere <math><mi>Q</mi></math> in <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and the string being taut (see figure). If sphere <math><mi>P</mi></math> alone in <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> has terminal velocity <math><msub><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></math> and <math><mi>Q</mi></math> alone in <math><msub><mrow><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> has terminal velocity <math><msub><mrow><mover accent=\"true\"><mrow><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>→</mo></mover></mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub></math> , then<br ><br/><img src=\"assets\\qt0020_37df5c16f035.jpg\"/></p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
